From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenCCU <contact@openccu.local>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 21:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pci: pcie-brcmstb: bcm2712 skip internal RP1 PCIe probe by
 default
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On Raspberry Pi 5, probing the internal RP1 PCIe host (pcie2) in U-Boot can
leave RP1 in a state where Linux later fails to claim BAR resources and the
onboard Ethernet does not appear.

Keep RP1-side PCIe probing disabled by default for BCM2712 while preserving
external NVMe PCIe probing. Existing `u-boot,no-probe` handling remains
supported and can still disable other nodes explicitly.

---
 drivers/pci/pcie_brcmstb.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/pcie_brcmstb.c b/drivers/pci/pcie_brcmstb.c
index cd2d395947a..e1469f8f0ae 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/pcie_brcmstb.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/pcie_brcmstb.c
@@ -682,6 +682,12 @@ static int brcm_pcie_of_to_plat(struct udevice *dev)
 
 	pcie->ssc = ofnode_read_bool(dn, "brcm,enable-ssc");
 	pcie->no_probe = ofnode_read_bool(dn, "u-boot,no-probe");
+	if (pcie->soc_base == BCM2712 &&
+	    !pcie->no_probe &&
+	    dev_read_addr(dev) == 0x1000120000ULL) {
+		printf("PCIe BRCM: BCM2712 internal RP1 host detected, skipping probe\n");
+		pcie->no_probe = true;
+	}
 
 	ret = ofnode_read_u32(dn, "max-link-speed", &max_link_speed);
 	if (ret < 0 || max_link_speed > 4)
-- 
